language-derived-from-the-record-6 = unlines (cons "**4. Meaning is transport.** For a participant i and a word w at a moment t, the selected occurrences Sel_i(w, t) are the past occurrences e of w in i's record whose context c(e) is identified, by a path p : c(e) = c_t, with the present context c_t. Each selected occurrence e came with what followed it, r(e): what i did next, what happened next, what was said next. The path p transports it to the present. The meaning of the present occurrence is the family M_i(w, t) = Σ_{(e,p) : Sel_i(w,t)} transport_p(r(e)). This derives the content of the paper's reception relation (1.4), Receive_i : S_i → U → S_i → A_i → 𝒰: Receive_i(s, w, s′, a) holds exactly when (s′, a) is a transported continuation of a selected occurrence. The meaning is determinate when the transported family is contractible, every selected continuation agreeing up to a path. An ambiguity is a family that is not contractible: one occurrence whose possible contexts transport different continuations. Context resolves an ambiguity by shrinking the fiber of selected occurrences, never by weighting it." nil)
